---
// The card grid (specs/pages/projects-index.md §2.3) — the overview
// archetype's native pattern, rendered on / and on /projects/.
//
// It is a component and not a class so the two call sites cannot drift.
// src/styles/projects.css opened with the reason and the reason is unchanged:
// §2.2's disclosure test — "no two cards with visually identical affordances
// produce different navigation outcomes" — is a property of the card, so there
// has to be exactly one card. Holding the rules in one stylesheet only ever
// got half of that; the DOM order and the class names still lived twice, kept
// the same by a comment asking the next editor to keep them that way. One
// component is the other half, and it is structural rather than advisory:
// there is one <ul>, one <li>, one set of affordances, and no page can spell a
// second.
//
// ── auto-fill, not auto-fit, and the difference is load-bearing ────────────
//
// auto-fill keeps the empty tracks, so two cards render at track width and
// stay start-aligned; auto-fit collapses them and two cards stretch across the
// measure — the exact failure §2.3 forbids ("two cards must not stretch to
// fill a three-column row"). auto-fit is the more commonly typed of the two,
// so a future edit to it will look like a no-op and will not be.
//
// That paragraph used to sit against the `grid-template-columns` declaration
// it explains, at projects.css:18-23. There is no utility spelling for
// repeat()/minmax(), so the whole track definition is now one arbitrary-value
// token in the class attribute below — less legible than the declaration was,
// and this comment is the compensation. Anyone editing that token is editing
// the thing this paragraph is about.
//
// ── the rest of the grid ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// `gap-x-8 gap-y-0` is the old `gap: 0 32px`: a column gutter and no row
// gutter. Rows need none, because each card draws its own hairline at its
// block-end edge (Card.astro).
//
// `justify-start` compiles to `justify-content: flex-start` rather than to the
// `start` keyword the stylesheet wrote. The CSS Box Alignment spec defines
// flex-start as behaving exactly as start outside a flex container, so in a
// grid container the two are the same declaration under two names; and 4.3.3
// has no arbitrary-value spelling for this property, so there is no third
// option to prefer.
---

<ul
  class="grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fill,minmax(280px,1fr))] justify-start gap-x-8 gap-y-0 list-none m-0 p-0"
>
  <slot />
</ul>
